.TH AGENTSHIELD 1 "2026-08-08" "AgentShield 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentshield \- local-first security scanner and memory auditor for AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentshield
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AgentShield inspects skills, MCP configuration, prompts, scripts, and stored memory without
executing target code. Every finding includes deterministic evidence and remediation. Scans are
local; nothing is uploaded in the Community edition.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan <target>
Static scan of a file or directory. Supports \fB--format\fP terminal|json|sarif|html|agentbom,
\fB--output\fP, \fB--policy\fP, and \fB--ci\fP.
.TP
.B scan-mcp <config>
Inspect an MCP server configuration for misleading tools and wildcard scopes.
.TP
.B permissions <target>
List the declared permission surface for a target.
.TP
.B diff <old> <new>
Risk-delta between two canonical scan reports.
.TP
.B policy check <report.json> <policy.yaml>
Evaluate a report against a policy file.
.TP
.B policy simulate <policy.yaml> <report.json...>
Simulate a policy across historical reports with \fB--json\fP and \fB--fail-on-block\fP.
.TP
.B report <report.json> \-\-format html
Render a self-contained HTML report.
.TP
.B rules list
List static and memory rules. \fB--json\fP for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B explain <ruleId>
Explain a static (\fBAS-SC-*\fP) or memory (\fBAS-ME-*\fP) rule.
.TP
.B baseline create|add|validate|prune
Manage reviewed, expiring finding suppressions.
.TP
.B memory audit <target>
Read-only memory audit. \fB--format\fP terminal|json|html|sarif|agentbom|bundle.
.TP
.B memory quarantine|restore <target> <memoryId>
Reversibly quarantine or restore a memory record without deleting the source.
.TP
.B persona create|create-text|list|show|render|apply|verify|applications|remove
Define, validate, render, and apply agent personas with a verifiable, hash-chained audit trail.
\fBpersona create <file.yaml> --actor <name>\fP registers a structured persona;
\fBpersona create-text <file.txt> --actor <name>\fP registers any raw text as a free-form persona
(id and name are derived; no YAML required). \fBpersona render <id>\fP renders the system prompt
with \fB--set name=value\fP overrides.
.TP
.B persona apply <id> \-\-actor <name>
Apply a persona: render, inject, and record an immutable application receipt (raw prompt is never
stored, only its hash). \fBpersona verify <file>\fP validates a definition without registering;
\fBpersona applications\fP lists receipts and verifies the chain.
.TP
.B persona model <id> \-\-provider <openai|anthropic|gemini|mistral|ollama|responses|generic> \-\-model <name> \-\-actor <name>
Apply a persona and emit a provider-native AI model request (OpenAI messages, Anthropic system,
Gemini systemInstruction, Mistral messages, Ollama messages + options, OpenAI Responses instructions,
or generic) as JSON, including the application receipt. Sampling options:
\fB--temperature\fP, \fB--max-tokens\fP, \fB--top-p\fP. No network call is made.
.TP
.B persona chat <id> \-\-provider <name> \-\-model <name> \-\-actor <name> \-\-message <text>
Apply a persona and send a live test message to the model with the operator's own API key (from
\fBOPENAI_API_KEY\fP/\fBANTHROPIC_API_KEY\fP/\fBGEMINI_API_KEY\fP/\fBMISTRAL_API_KEY\fP or
\fB--api-key\fP; never persisted) and print the model's reply. \fB--base-url\fP is required for the
generic provider; Ollama is local and needs no key. This is the only outbound call in the CLI and
is explicit, opt-in, and operator-initiated.
.TP
.B runtime ingest|trace
Ingest sanitized runtime events and build a source-to-action evidence graph.
.TP
.B telemetry status|enable|disable|preview
Manage local telemetry consent. Off by default; nothing is transmitted.
.TP
.B completion <bash|zsh|fish>
Print a shell completion script.
.SH EXIT CODES
0 pass, 1 operational failure, 2 block/severity failure, 3 required review, 4 incomplete CI analysis.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .agentshield/
Local data directory for reports, memory cache, quarantine snapshots, runtime events, and telemetry
consent. Created on demand and never uploaded.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
agentshield scan ./my-skill --format sarif --output agentshield.sarif --ci
.PP
agentshield memory audit memories.jsonl --format bundle --output bundle.json
.PP
agentshield telemetry preview
.SH SEE ALSO
